Subject: pcre2test: keep the exit status when built with POSIX exit semantics on VMS

pcre2test always returns SS$_NORMAL on VMS and reports results through DCL
symbols.  Built with _POSIX_EXIT (/MAIN=POSIX_EXIT), SS$_NORMAL (1) becomes
exit code 1, so every run looked like a failure.  Keep the C exit value then.

--- a/src/pcre2test.c	2026-10-03 11:06:16.559321812 +0100
+++ b/src/pcre2test.c	2026-10-03 11:06:16.581712526 +0100
@@ -4458,7 +4458,10 @@
 free(tables3);
 free_globals();
 
-#if defined(__VMS)
+/* With POSIX exit semantics (_POSIX_EXIT, /MAIN=POSIX_EXIT) the exit status
+is the C value, as on other systems, so keep yield; otherwise values are
+returned via DCL symbols. */
+#if defined(__VMS) && !defined(_POSIX_EXIT)
   yield = SS$_NORMAL;  /* Return values via DCL symbols */
 #endif
 
